or:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      )</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"submit\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>Sign up&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">form</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>What makes this good:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>When:</strong> errors appear after leaving the field (<code>onBlur</code>) or submitting, not while the user is still typing their first letter.</li>\n<li><strong>What:</strong> the message says how to fix it, not just &quot;Invalid&quot;.</li>\n<li><strong>Accessible:</strong> <code>aria-invalid</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> link the message to the field, and <code>role=&quot;alert&quot;</code> announces it to screen readers.</li>\n<li><strong>Reset:</strong> after a successful submit, clear the value <strong>and</strong> the touched flag, or the error shows again on the empty field.</li>\n<li><code>noValidate</code> turns off the browser&#39;s own popups, so your messages are the only ones.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Always validate again on the <strong>server</strong>: anyone can send any request, whatever your form allows.</p>\n<h2 id=\"uncontrolled-inputs\">Uncontrolled Inputs</h2>\n<p>You don&#39;t always need state for every field. For a simple form you only read on submit, let the DOM keep the values and read them with <code>FormData</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> handleSubmit</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">event</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  event.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">preventDefault</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> FormData</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(event.currentTarget);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">  onSearch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(data.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"query\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">form</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onSubmit</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">handleSubmit</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">input</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"query\"</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> defaultValue</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">form</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Use <code>defaultValue</code> (not <code>value</code>) for uncontrolled inputs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"form-libraries\">Form Libraries</h2>\n<p>For big forms with many rules, a library saves a lot of code:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>React Hook Form:</strong> fast, uses uncontrolled inputs under the hood, works well with schema validation.</li>\n<li><strong>Zod</strong> or <strong>Valibot:</strong> describe the rules once as a schema, and use the same schema on the server.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>A controlled input gets <code>value</code> from state and updates it in <code>onChange</code>.</li>\n<li>Handle <code>onSubmit</code> on the form and call <code>preventDefault</code>.</li>\n<li>Checkboxes use <code>checked</code>; many fields fit in one state object updated by <code>name</code>.</li>\n<li>Compute errors from values, show them after blur or submit, link them with <code>aria-describedby</code>, and validate on the server too.</li>\n<li>Use uncontrolled inputs with <code>FormData</code> for simple forms, and React Hook Form with a schema for large ones.</li>\n</ol>\n"}